WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
It’s 10:04 in Kolkata. You’re coordinating
a client demo that starts at 10:24.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:10.500
Rahul opens the recovery thread.
The demo server is unresponsive.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.270
Alex’s client update arrives while
Rahul’s original request stays open.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.300
Give Rahul the recovery check
and ask for a checkpoint.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.300
The task board shows Rahul as owner.
The recovery check is in progress.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.600
Follow the task back to Rahul’s
original request and reply.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:33.320
Give Alex confirmed facts and promise
an update at 10:15 IST.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:38.950
The calendar shows the 10:15 checkpoint.
Server recovery remains unconfirmed.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.810
Approved budget, ₹18,000.
Vendor draft, ₹22,000.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:50.250
Hold the draft for review and ask Meera
to reconcile the ₹4,000 difference.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:56.250
The practice feedback lists strengths
and a skill to practise next.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.290
Open the fictional recruiter view
to see the three separate findings.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:05.850
Client communication links to Alex’s
request, your reply and what changed.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.000
Try the coordinator’s desk yourself.
Play again lets you start a fresh run.
